---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_URL } from "../../consts";

const personJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  "@id": `${SITE_URL}/author/mireia/#person`,
  name: "Mireia",
  url: `${SITE_URL}/author/mireia/`,
  jobTitle: "Power BI author and model builder",
  description:
    "Author and maintainer of powerbitutorials.com, writing about Power BI, DAX and Power Query.",
  knowsAbout: ["Power BI", "DAX", "Power Query", "Data modeling", "Business intelligence"],
  worksFor: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mireia — Author"
  description="Mireia writes and maintains every tutorial on powerbitutorials.com, covering Power BI, DAX, Power Query and data modeling with tested examples."
  article={true}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personJsonLd)} />

  <article class="about-page">
    <div class="content-width">
      <span class="page-eyebrow">Author</span>
      <h1>Mireia</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Author and maintainer of powerbitutorials.com. Every tutorial on this site is written and
        reviewed by the same person.
      </p>

      <div class="author-card">
        <div class="author-avatar" aria-hidden="true">M</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Power BI author &amp; model builder</h3>
          <p>Writes about the parts of Power BI that take the longest to get right.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What I write about</h2>
      <p>
        The articles here concentrate on the mechanisms underneath the clicks: how filter context
        and context transition actually work, why a star schema makes DAX shorter, and which Power
        Query steps quietly break query folding. Those are the places where copying a formula from
        a forum answer stops working as soon as your model changes shape.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Every DAX and Power Query snippet is run against a sample model in Power BI Desktop before
          it is published. If it does not return the stated result, it does not ship.
        </li>
        <li>
          Version-dependent behaviour is stated explicitly and linked to the Microsoft documentation
          so you can check it against your own build.
        </li>
        <li>
          When a feature is renamed, deprecated or superseded, the article is revised and its review
          date is updated rather than left to drift.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections and topic requests</h2>
      <p>
        If a formula fails on your model, or a step assumes something you don't have, that is a bug
        in the article — <a href="/contact">send it over</a> and it gets fixed. Topic requests are
        read too; the queue is driven by what readers keep getting stuck on.
      </p>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <a href="/tutorials" class="btn btn-primary">Browse all tutorials</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { padding: 56px 0 80px; }
  .page-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .about-page h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .about-page h2 { margin-top: 2.5em; }
  .about-page ul { padding-left: 1.4em; }
  .about-page li { margin-bottom: 0.7em; }
  .author-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 20px;
    background: var(--c-bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .author-avatar {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c-accent);
    color: var(--c-accent-text);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 800;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .author-card h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .author-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .about-cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 11px 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--c-accent); color: var(--c-accent-text); }
  .btn-secondary { background: var(--c-bg); color: var(--c-text); border-color: var(--c-border); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about-page h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
    .author-card { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
    .about-cta { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
